        <ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00831-w">
            <ns1:title>Towards global nutrient justice via a circular bionutrient economy</ns1:title>
            <ns1:link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00831-w</ns1:link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Reviews Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 17 September 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43017-026-00831-w"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43017-026-00831-w&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Nutrient management is central to global food security, ecosystem health and climate resilience, yet current practices are profoundly inequitable and unsustainable. This Perspective introduces the circular bionutrient economy as a justice-oriented framework for advancing ecological balance and social equity through the recycling of organic waste streams into agrifood systems.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Towards global nutrient justice via a circular bionutrient economy</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Chuan Liao</dc:creator><dc:creator>Shuai Zhou</dc:creator><dc:creator>Seongmin Shin</dc:creator><dc:creator>Danning Lu</dc:creator><dc:creator>Yujin Lee</dc:creator><dc:creator>Shuai Xu</dc:creator><dc:creator>Ying Tu</dc:creator><dc:creator>Krisztina Mosdossy</dc:creator><dc:creator>Lucinda Li</dc:creator><dc:creator>Rebecca Nelson</dc:creator><dc:creator>Johannes Lehmann</dc:creator>
